# General Guidelines

- Always answer questions directly first
- Use actual workspace paths in docs, scripts, and examples; do not use placeholder paths like `/path/to/project`
- Never make code changes without explicit user request
- Comment and documentation rules live in `documentation-standards.mdc`

## Solution Structure

Projects live at the repo root, one per layer:

| Project                      | Role                                                              |
|------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------|
| `NTierTemplate/`             | Shared types, message contracts, domain entities, DAO interfaces  |
| `NTierTemplate.Application/` | Use-case orchestration, application services, common IoC wiring   |
| `NTierTemplate.Data/`        | EF entities, DbContext, DAO implementations, Identity persistence |
| `NTierTemplate.Api/`         | ASP.NET Core HTTP API (host + IoC bootstrap)                      |
| `NTierTemplate.Cli/`         | Command-line entry points (host + IoC bootstrap)                  |
| `NTierTemplate.Queue/`       | RabbitMQ worker host (host + IoC bootstrap)                       |
| `NTierTemplate.Web/`         | Angular client                                                    |
| `NTierTemplate.Test/`        | Unit tests — references Domain and Application only               |

Within each project, organize by **domain**, not technical folders (`controllers/`, `services/`, `views/`, etc.).

All **non-configuration logic** lives in Domain and Application. Entry points, Data, and hosts are configuration and wiring — not unit-tested.

## Layer Dependencies

Project references stack upward from **Domain** at the bottom. `NTierTemplate.Web/` is outside this graph — it talks to the API over HTTP only.

Each entry-point host (`Api`, `Cli`, `Queue`) bootstraps its own IoC container. **Application owns the common wiring** — shared `ServiceCollection` extension methods that register Data, DAOs, and application services. Hosts call Application's registration; they do not duplicate it.

```
    Api · Cli · Queue        entry-point hosts (IoC bootstrap per host)
            │
       Application           use cases + common ServiceCollection wiring
            │
           Data              DAO implementations, EF, Identity
            │
          Domain             types, message contracts, entity behavior

Web ──HTTP──▶ Api            (outside project-reference graph)
```

| Project                      | Project references          |
|------------------------------|-----------------------------|
| `NTierTemplate/`             | (none)                      |
| `NTierTemplate.Data/`        | Domain                      |
| `NTierTemplate.Application/` | Domain, Data                |
| `NTierTemplate.Api/`         | Domain, Application         |
| `NTierTemplate.Cli/`         | Domain, Application         |
| `NTierTemplate.Queue/`       | Domain, Application         |
| `NTierTemplate.Test/`        | Domain, Application         |
| `NTierTemplate.Web/`         | *(none — HTTP client only)* |

Entry points must not take a project reference to **Data**. They consume behavior through Application services and shared types from Domain — not EF types, DAO implementations, or Identity managers.

